rmat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIOKA, YOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASE, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUHARA, TADAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel flame-retardant resin composition comprising: (A) 100 parts by weight of a thermoplastic resin which is not a thermotropic liquid-crystal polymer; (B) 0.01 to 50 parts by weight of a thermotropic liquid-crystal polymer; and (C) 1 to 30 parts by weight of a nonhalogenated phosphazene compound. The composition is free from any problem caused by the use of a halogenated compound, is excellent in flame retardancy, mechanical properties, moldability, etc., and is less apt to drip.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur une nouvelle composition de résine ignifuge comprenant: (A) 100 parties en poids d'une résine thermoplastique qui n'est pas un polymère liquide-cristal thermotropique; (B) 0,01 à 50 parties en poids d'un polymère liquide-cristal thermotropique; et (C) 1 à 30 parties en poids d'un composé de phosphazène non halogéné. Tout problème que pourrait provoquer le composé halogéné est ainsi évité et la composition présente d'excellentes propriétés ignifuges, mécaniques et une excellente aptitude au moulage, etc., et risque moins de baver.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the